Refactored `ClosingFuture` internals in both [`guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java:1082) and [`android/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/android/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java:1076). The main change was extracting shared helpers for the “create temporary closeables, run work, then merge them” flow, which removed duplicated logic from `submitAsync`, `Peeker.call`, `Peeker.callAsync`, and `CloseableList`’s sync/async application paths. You can see the shared helpers at [`callWithNewCloseables` and `callAsyncWithNewCloseables`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java:1093), and one of the simplified call sites at [`submitAsync`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java:415).

I also centralized the end-of-pipeline state checks in [`State.prepareToFinalize` and `invalidFinalizationState`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/guava/src/com/google/common/util/concurrent/ClosingFuture.java:2215), which replaces the duplicated `switch(status.get())` branches in `finishToFuture` and `finishToValueAndCloser` while preserving the same error messages and transition behavior.

Verification was limited to static checks: `git diff --check` passed. I could not run the `ClosingFuture` tests here because this environment still has no usable Maven runtime or wrapper jar.

